			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1733,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Route all notification atoms to canonical Vine crate\n\nReplace the local `super::Notification::*` dispatch in `MountainVinegRPCService.rs` with direct calls to `::Vine::Server::Notification::*`, collapsing the Mountain-local notification modules in `Source/Vine/Server/Notification/mod.rs` to only the three Mountain-specific utilities: `Support`, `OutputChannelCoalesce`, and `TerminalEnvCollection`.\n\nAll 46+ wired notification handlers — extension lifecycle, progress reporting, output channels, webview/terminal lifecycle, SCM registration, language providers, debug/status-bar/decoration APIs — are now thin pass-throughs that delegate to the canonical implementations in the Vine library crate. This finalizes the extraction of Cocoon→Mountain IPC logic from Mountain into the shared gRPC protocol layer.\n\nMountain's `send_cocoon_notification` dispatcher is reduced to a pure routing table with no inline logic, and the Notification module no longer re-exports the full atom suite, enforcing Vine as the single source of truth for IPC contracts.",
			"SHA": "d3b63235b1e7a8560b093a2ca8e21096c02f14cd"
		}
